{
  "$comment": "S-3 STORIES ×4 (owner 2026-10-28: 'agent stories as a new way the agent communicates ... decisions/questions and results land here, instagram-story-like UI ... swipeable. all questions and drafts propagate to the top. minimal text ... default to visual only'). Stories REPLACE the Guide tab and the Dock's plan/question rows. A STORY = a session's OWN show card (`messages` row with author_session_id = session_id, card kind `plan` | `question` | `surface`, posted by `exponential_show`) that is a story: `card.story` true, or `card.story` absent and (kind plan|question, or a resolved picture). A plan/question with `questionId` (an engine's relay ask) and an `ask` mirror never are. KIND: plan → `plan`, question → `question`, surface → `result`. A plan waits while `decision` is null (any decision, `superseded` included, = gone); a question waits while `answeredAt` and `answer` are both null (answered = gone). A result is kept while age (now − createdAt) < `constants.unseenHours` hours when unseen, < `constants.seenHours` when seen. SEEN = createdAt <= the viewer's mark of the story's ROOT: max(session_reads.read_at, session_reads.story_seen_at) of the row (user = viewer, session = rootId); no row = unseen. A host marks a story seen when it is SHOWN in the viewer: `sessions.markStoriesSeen({sessionId: rootId, at: createdAt})`, the server keeps the greatest. RINGS = `stories(input)`: one ring per AGENT (key `agent:<id>`: the root's own agentId (its agent conversation) else the root's startedByAgentId; title = the agent's name, `assistant` from the host's agent row) and one per ROOT chat with no agent (key `root:<rootId>`; title = the root's name). A ring's stories: waiting first, then unseen, then seen, each group oldest first (createdAt, then id), so the viewer opens on what needs the person. A ring: `waiting` = its waiting count, `unseen` = any story waiting or unseen. RING ORDER: the Assistant's ring first (whatever its state), then rings with waiting, then rings with unseen, then the rest, each group by its newest story (createdAt desc, then key). A ring with no story left is absent. A STORY (out): id (the message id), sessionId, rootId, sessionName (the posting session's name), kind, waiting, seen, createdAt, meta = '<copy kind> · <age>' (age: < 1 min `now`, < 60 min `<m>m`, < 24 h `<h>h`, else `<d>d`, floored), title = a result's card title, a question's text, a plan's first plain line (ask-dock `askDockTitle`), else null; pictures = the card's RESOLVED pictures (attachmentId set) in card order {label, attachmentId, width, height, caption}; surface = the card has a surface; text = a plan's markdown when it has neither a picture nor a surface, else null; footer = `plan` (THE plan options of ask-dock.json: Approve = approve, Change = reject + its feedback field) | `choices` (a question with options: its option chips, + the free-text field when custom) | `reply` (a question with no options: the free-text field) | `none` (a result); autoAdvanceMs = `constants.autoAdvanceMs` for a result, else null (a decision never advances on its own). An answer goes through THE card-answer path (`sessions.answer`, the same as the in-chat card); the story then drops out (answered). STORY RING (styleguide `story-ring`, eUI `StoryRing`: an avatar inside a ring split into one arc per story, `ring.gap` degrees apart, `ring.width` px; a waiting story's arc = the plan/question tint (ask-dock tints), an unseen one = foreground, a seen one = the glass-stroke hairline): the chats header's agent bubbles (chats.json BUBBLES) wear their agent's ring; a tap on a bubble with a ring opens THE viewer at that ring (no ring = the interim chats.json tap); the root rings follow the agent bubbles in the same row (the root's session avatar, its name under it). STORY VIEWER (styleguide `story-viewer`; Exponential-specific, not eUI): phones (iOS, Android, web-mobile) = full screen over everything; web wide + the IDE = a centered modal (`viewer.width` × `viewer.height` max, `viewer.radius`) over a scrim on the list. Top: THE StoryProgress (eUI `StoryProgress`: one segment per story of the ring, `progress.gap` apart, `progress.height` tall; done = foreground, the current = its fill fraction, todo = the glass-stroke track). Header: the ring's avatar (agent mark / session avatar), the story's `sessionName`, `meta` muted, the close ghost glyph; a tap on the avatar or name opens that session (the #1309 back stack) and closes the viewer. Body: the pictures (fitted, a horizontal pager when several, the caption under it) and/or the surface (THE surface card renderer of chats.json `surfaceCard`), else the plan text (markdown); the title over the body in one line when present. Footer: per `footer`; nothing for a result. NAVIGATION: tap the right third / swipe left / ArrowRight / the side arrow (wide) = next story, past the last = the next ring, past the last ring = close; left third / swipe right / ArrowLeft = previous (the first story of a ring = the previous ring's last); swipe down / Escape / the close glyph = close; holding a press pauses the timer. Only a result advances on its own after `autoAdvanceMs`. TOOL: `exponential_show {story?}`: default true for ask/plan/pictures, false for a plain surface (a status card stays in the chat only); a surface may carry `pictures` (labels; each returned curl uploads one) so a result story shows screenshots. PR BODIES read the stories: pr-body.json `storyCases`. Mirrors: desktop domain::stories, iOS ExpCore Stories.swift, Android domain/Stories.kt replay `cases` comparing the WHOLE expected array.",
  "constants": {
    "seenHours": 24,
    "unseenHours": 168,
    "autoAdvanceMs": 6000
  },
